# sdmbench environment variables. Copy to `.env` and edit.
#
# `.env` is gitignored. NEVER commit real credentials.
# sdmbench never embeds, requests or transmits credentials, and never bypasses
# an authentication or licence gate.

# --- cache -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Where datasets, embeddings, model checkpoints, upstream clones and run
# outputs live. Defaults to ~/.cache/sdmbench (or %LOCALAPPDATA%\sdmbench\Cache).
# Point this at fast local storage; a full benchmark writes thousands of files.
# SDMBENCH_CACHE=/scratch/$USER/sdmbench

# --- R ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Needed for the published MaxNet / BRT / GAM / Random Forest baselines.
# Only set this if Rscript is not on PATH (common on Windows).
# SDMBENCH_RSCRIPT=C:\Program Files\R\R-4.3.2\bin\Rscript.exe

# --- GPU -------------------------------------------------------------------
# CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0
# OMP_NUM_THREADS=8

# --- Hugging Face ----------------------------------------------------------
# The TabPFN-SDM checkpoints are under the Prior Labs License v1.1. Accept it on
# the model page first, then authenticate with `huggingface-cli login` — which
# stores the token in ~/.cache/huggingface, NOT here. A token is only needed for
# gated repositories.
# HF_HOME=/scratch/$USER/huggingface

# --- Google Earth Engine (AlphaEarth embeddings) ---------------------------
# Requires YOUR OWN Earth Engine account. Run `earthengine authenticate` first;
# credentials are stored by the Earth Engine client, not by sdmbench.
# SDMBENCH_EE_PROJECT=your-gcp-project-id

# --- NASA Earthdata (MODIS, planned) ---------------------------------------
# Use a ~/.netrc entry rather than environment variables — that is the
# mechanism NASA's services expect, and it keeps the secret out of the process
# environment.
